{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LBep1JvQuLhSV1RYfp6vmp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Rust translation of the C library in `c_src/` (a trimmed derivative of\n2\t//! `cute_png.h` by Randy Gaul -- zlib / public-domain licensed, see\n3\t//! `c_src/license.txt`).\n4\t//!\n5\t//! The translation is intentionally *literal*: every observable behaviour of\n6\t//! the C code (including its quirks and bugs, evaluation/validation order,\n7\t//! integer wrap-around, pointer arithmetic and out-of-bounds accesses) is\n8\t//! reproduced so that the exported ABI is byte-for-byte compatible.\n9\t//!\n10\t//! The C build compiles with `NDEBUG` semantics for the purposes of this\n11\t//! translation, i.e. the `assert()` calls sprinkled through the original code\n12\t//! are treated as no-ops (they are documented in comments where they appear).\n13\t//! Everything else is mirrored exactly, which is why shifts use the wrapping\n14\t//! forms (matching what x86-64 code generation does for C's UB cases) and why\n15\t//! table lookups go through raw pointers (matching C's unchecked indexing).\n16\t\n17\t#![allow(\n18\t    non_camel_case_types,\n19\t    non_upper_case_globals,\n20\t    non_snake_case,\n21\t    unused_assignments,\n22\t    unused_variables,\n23\t    dead_code\n24\t)]\n25\t\n26\tuse core::ffi::{CStr, c_char, c_int, c_void};\n27\tuse core::ptr;\n28\t\n29\tunsafe extern \"C\" {\n30\t    fn malloc(size: usize) -> *mut c_void;\n31\t    fn calloc(nmemb: usize, size: usize) -> *mut c_void;\n32\t    fn free(ptr: *mut c_void);\n33\t    fn memcpy(dest: *mut c_void, src: *const c_void, n: usize) -> *mut c_void;\n34\t    fn memset(dest: *mut c_void, c: c_int, n: usize) -> *mut c_void;\n35\t    fn memcmp(s1: *const c_void, s2: *const c_void, n: usize) -> c_int;\n36\t}\n37\t\n38\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n39\t// Public types (include/lib.h)\n40\t// -------------------------------