{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DGZ1G2KhTv8X7L94yqoTMb","type":"tool_result","content":"--- c_src unchanged check ---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9254ee7d-2c80-4fca-a947-c2f2f393fc6d","uuid":"dab7569a-b346-480c-bcce-c09b23633134","timestamp":"2026-08-29T14:11:57.421Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"--- c_src unchanged check ---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5nhjtisvxcsjdmwoibf4urhzqfejmmhlfvcdceyixa6ttzaptqgq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What was wrong with the translation\n\nThree **real** correctness bugs, all rooted in mischaracterizing the reference build:\n\n1. **`assert()` is live, not compiled out.** `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the reference `.so` is `-O0` **without `NDEBUG`** (it imports `__assert_fail`). The prior translation treated all ten asserts as no-ops, so malformed DEFLATE data returned an error where the C dies with `SIGABRT`. E.g. `cp_inflate(in, 0, out, n)` aborts on `assert(s->bits_left > 0)`. → added `c_assert!` → `abort()` at all ten sites.\n\n2. **The `.data` layout model was backwards.** `cp_block` indexes `cp_len_*`/`cp_dist_*` out of range with corrupt trees, reading whatever the linker placed next. `objdump -s -j .data` shows **source order** (`cp_fixed_table` @0, … `cp_dist_base` @544), not the reverse order the model assumed — so every out-of-range read returned the wrong byte (`cp_len_extra_bits[32]` is 3, not 16). Fixed, plus modelled the two `.bss` objects behind `.data`.\n\n3. **`cp_dynamic`'s stack overrun wasn't modelled.** Its 16/17/18 run-length symbols push `n` up to 137 entries past `lens[320]`, aliasing `lenlens`, `sym`, `nlen`, `ndst`, `nlit` and `n` itself in the `-O0` frame. Zeroing `nlit`/`ndst` changes the loop bound and the trailing `cp_build` calls. Replaced the padded-array approximation with a byte-exact frame model derived from `objdump -d`.\n\nAlso: `cp_build`'s `counts[16]` overrun is provably always followed by its own `assert(len < 16)`, and `lens[-1]` is provably the MSB of the spilled `s` pointer (= 0) rather than indeterminate — both now documented instead of guessed.\n\n## Results\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `diff` of sorted `nm -D --defined-only` is **empty** (9 symbols); 0 unexpected undefined |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 52 rows, all pass across randomized inputs |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 27 graceful + 10 assert + 10 boundary rows, all pass; 6 rows proven unreachable with the argument recorded |\n| feature combos | no `[features]` declared → `default` and `--no-default-features`, both green |\n\nHarness: `tests/harness/` `dlopen`s both `.so`s, runs every call in a forked child (so `Signal(6)` vs `Ret(bytes)` is a comparable outcome), restores table mutations per case, disables core dumps, and applies a per-case `SIGALRM` watchdog. Fuzzers compared ~3400 mutated inputs with **0 divergences**; `fuzz_same` first runs the C twice and drops the handful of cases where the C disagrees with itself (heap overflows and uninitialised-`malloc` reads — documented as out of scope).\n\n`c_src/` is untouched. `./run_verification.sh` reproduces everything."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":416534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":278,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9254ee7d-2c80-4fca-a947-c2f2f393fc6d","uuid":"daa016fe-9c11-4c0b-8186-d4b0204d315e","timestamp":"2026-08-29T14:12:14.704Z"}
